    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d404">

                <pb facs="0390" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg370"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 52.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 29, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of 4th November last (No. 53)
                    has been received. The part which you have taken in regard to Mr. Pumpelly’s
                    exploration with a view to <pb facs="0391" n="371" xml:id="pg371"/> the
                    discovery and development of coal mines in the region near Peking is approved
                    and commended.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
